5,1,1,talk,Midori,,I worry about programs that collapse in year two. I want to see where recent starts actually broke down.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,I am concerned about which past initiatives actually helped patients. I want to review what earlier attempts produced before adding another.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I need to understand how staffing pressure shifts when a new program launches. I will look at the ward nursing vacancies and agency cover.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is a one-time gift, not a promise. I need to know what this allocation actually covers before we commit to anything.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shizue,,I am curious how a new program fits into the daily flow. I want to see the booking system records and room coverage.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, that is a fair point. I am also checking the board minutes on the jointly run clinic to see how that arrangement held up.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, I agree. I will look at the readmission figures from the call-back trial to see if that earlier effort actually reduced returns.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, readmission data is useful, but I am focused on who actually covers the shifts. I will check the therapy and midwifery staffing review.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, staffing is a recurring cost, not a capital one. I will check the ledger to see what is actually left after the initial build.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I understand your caution. I will also look at the regional fund tariffs to see how travel costs affect patient access.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, staffing gaps are often the first sign of trouble. I will check the data agreements with outside surgeries to see if those partners are truly committed.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, staffing is vital, but I need to know if the work actually reached patients. I will check the visit completion on the shared nursing round.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, travel costs matter, but the human element is often overlooked. I will check the ward nursing vacancies and agency cover.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, tariffs are a variable, not a fixed cost. I will check the ledger to see the actual development allocation.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I hear you. The human element is crucial. I will check the rooms, parking and shuttle coverage to see if the physical space can handle the extra load.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Midori,,I will check the board minutes on the jointly run clinic and the data agreements with outside surgeries.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
