35,2,1,talk,Midori,,The jointly run clinic collapsed because neither department owned the rota. I am worried about shared responsibilities.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The call-back trial reduced readmissions by a fifth, but only while it ran. I need to know if that effort actually stuck.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Nine unfilled posts and rising agency costs. The therapy review shows physios leaving, but midwifery has slack. I need to see how that imbalance affects new programs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,The allocation is down a quarter. Off-site contacts earn nothing. We need a program that generates revenue on-site to survive.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The booking system only tracks named slots. Unplanned work vanishes. The car park fills by eleven, and the shuttle misses most villages.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, that revenue gap is critical. If a program relies on outside partners, the fourteen-month agreement delay makes it impossible to launch on time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the shared round lost a third of visits to access barriers. If patients cannot reach us, the program fails before it starts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, the agency costs are eating the budget. A program needing extra therapy staff will just add to the vacancy problem.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, access is a tariff issue. If we bill on-site, we capture the revenue. Off-site is a financial black hole.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, access is indeed a barrier. But the car park is full by eleven. We must ensure the new program does not clog the existing flow.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, the staffing imbalance is real. If we add a program needing physios, we are just deepening the hole. I worry about that strain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, the shared round lost a third of visits to access barriers. If patients cannot reach us, the program fails before it starts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, exactly. The midwifery slack is a rare asset. We should not waste it on a program that needs scarce physios.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, the data agreements are a liability. I need to see the actual tariff capture before we approve any off-site model.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I agree. We must protect the midwifery slack. I am worried the new program will just add to the existing congestion.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,I am ready to see the candidates. We need a model that does not depend on fragile external partnerships or scarce staff.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am ready to see the candidates. We must choose something that actually reaches patients, not just another quiet initiative that fades away.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I am ready to see the candidates. We must pick a program that fits the current staffing reality, not one that ignores the vacancies.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I am ready. The numbers are clear. We need a program that pays for itself on-site, or it is a waste of the reduced allocation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am ready to see the candidates. We must choose a program that fits gently into our current flow, without causing the system to seize up.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
