60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Candidate D uses midwifery, which Misaki says has slack. It avoids the scarce physios and external data agreements. It feels like the most stable choice for us.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Candidate A mirrors the call-back trial that actually reduced readmissions. It reaches patients where they are, unlike the shared round that failed on access.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Candidate D fits the midwifery slack perfectly. It avoids the physio shortage and the agency costs I flagged. It is the only option that respects our current staffing reality.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Candidate A is a financial black hole. Off-site visits earn zero tariff. With the allocation down a quarter, we cannot afford a program that generates no on-site revenue.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Candidate D fits the midwifery slack. But the car park is full by eleven. Will the new classes just add to the morning congestion?,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, that is a valid concern. But D is scheduled, not walk-in. We can stagger the classes to avoid the eleven o'clock peak.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, the call-back trial proved that reaching patients at home works. The readmission drop was real. We cannot ignore that evidence just because the tariff is zero.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, the tariff is zero, but the agency bill is not. D uses existing midwifery slack, avoiding the expensive cover I flagged.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, the readmission drop is a statistic, not a budget line. If A generates no tariff, it is a permanent drain on our reduced allocation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I appreciate the thought. Staggering helps, but the booking system only tracks named slots. We must ensure D has fixed, bookable times so it does not vanish from our records.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, you are right. Fixed slots are essential. I will ensure D is booked as distinct, named appointments so the system captures every visit clearly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, the trial proved the model works. But the shared round failed on access. A must solve that barrier, or it is just another quiet failure.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, the agency bill is the real drain. D uses existing midwifery slack, avoiding the expensive cover I flagged. It is the only option that respects our current staffing reality.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, slack is not a strategy. D generates on-site tariff, unlike A. It is the only option that respects the ledger.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree. D generates on-site revenue. But we must ensure the parking and shuttle can handle the extra foot traffic without disrupting the existing flow.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I am ready to vote. Candidate D respects our staffing reality and generates on-site revenue. It is the most stable path forward for our team.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am ready to vote. Candidate A is the only one with proven patient impact. I will vote for A, hoping we can solve the access barriers.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I am ready to vote. Candidate D is the only choice that aligns with our staffing reality. I will vote for D.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,I am ready to vote. Candidate D is the only option that generates on-site tariff. It respects the reduced allocation and avoids the financial black hole of off-site visits.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am ready to vote. Candidate D fits our flow best. With fixed slots and staggered times, it will not seize up our already busy day.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
